---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="Privacy" kicker="Datenschutz" noindex>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: 28 October 2026</p>

  <h2>Short version</h2>
  <p>
    Finevelo has no advertising, no cookies, no cross-site tracking and no social media plugins. The public site loads no
    fonts, scripts or images from third parties. We count page views with our own cookieless analytics, which stores no IP
    addresses and cannot recognise you from one day to the next. Our host processes the technical access data needed to
    deliver the pages.
  </p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Vinati GmbH, Max-Eyth-Str. 7, 71364 Winnenden, Germany, represented by its managing director Manuel Walker. Contact
    details are in the <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and access data</h2>
  <p>
    The site is static and hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco,
    CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser sends technical data to GitHub's servers: IP address, date and time,
    the page requested, referrer, browser and operating system. GitHub uses this data to deliver the site and to protect it
    against attacks and abuse. We have no access to these logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (our legitimate interest in a secure, working website). The data may be processed in the
    USA. GitHub participates in the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, on which the transfer is based (Art. 45 GDPR). Details:
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub
    General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We set no cookies. If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so
    the site remembers it. It never leaves your device, and you can delete it in your browser settings at any time. This is
    strictly necessary for a function you asked for (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).
  </p>

  <h2>Page view statistics</h2>
  <p>
    To see which articles are read, each page view sends one request to our own statistics service. It records the page,
    the referring website (domain only), a rough device class based on screen width (phone, tablet, computer), the browser
    language and the time. No cookies are set and nothing is stored on or read from your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    To count unique visitors, a short code is computed from your IP address, your browser identifier and a random value that
    changes every day. Only this code is stored, never the IP address. The daily random value is deleted after two days, so
    the code cannot be traced back to you and you cannot be recognised across days. Statistics are kept for 13 months.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your browser sends a "Do Not Track" or Global Privacy Control signal, no request is sent at all. Legal basis: Art.
    6(1)(f) GDPR (our legitimate interest in knowing which content is read, using as little data as possible). You can object
    at any time (see below).
  </p>
  <p>
    The service runs on Supabase (Supabase, Inc.) on servers in Frankfurt, Germany, as our processor under a data processing
    agreement (Art. 28 GDPR). As Supabase is a US company, access from the USA cannot be completely ruled out; such transfers
    are covered by the EU Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 46 GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we process your address and message to answer you (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR for enquiries about a contract,
    otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). We delete them when the matter is settled, unless we are legally required to keep them.
  </p>

  <h2>Builders and shops directory</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/builders/">directory</a> lists businesses with the information they publish themselves: name, address,
    website and services, with a link to the public source. Where a business is run by a sole trader, this can be personal
    data. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (our interest in informing readers, and theirs in being found). Businesses can ask
    us at any time to correct or remove their entry.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Articles link to manufacturers, shops and sources. Those sites only receive data once you click a link, and their own
    privacy notices apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial tools</h2>
  <p>
    Our editors sign in to an internal editing tool. Their login data are processed by Supabase (servers in Frankfurt,
    Germany) and GitHub. This concerns only our editorial team, not readers.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing
    (Art. 18) and data portability (Art. 20). <strong>You can object at any time to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR
    (Art. 21).</strong> To exercise these rights, contact us using the details in the <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also complain to a data protection authority, for example the one responsible for us: Der Landesbeauftragte für
    den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Baden-Württemberg, Lautenschlagerstraße 20, 70173 Stuttgart, Germany.
  </p>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .updated {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
